From 861f84c7757d7bd3d94c9ad797701c987fd94179 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JingMatrix <jingmatrix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 22:51:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 25/47] Rework the WebUI key and log views

Stored keys: present each key with its class, algorithm and purposes, show the
keybox only when one is attributed (dropping the empty line otherwise), and
replace the funnel with a plain Spoofed / All toggle that reads more clearly.

Logs: a proper log viewer with a save sheet - the daemon writes the file itself
(a path-traversal-safe POST /logs/write) and a browser can download the tail over
GET /logs/download, which authenticates by a ?token= query parameter because a
navigation cannot set the header token every other route uses.

KeyAdmin serves each connection on its own thread with a read timeout and logs
every request. A client-supplied Content-Length is capped before it is used as an
allocation size, so a bogus value cannot force a huge allocation and take the
per-connection thread down with an OutOfMemoryError. Deleting a profile now
persists to disk immediately, bypassing the whole-config validation gate: a
removal cannot introduce invalidity, and the gate would otherwise reject it when a
different profile happened to be invalid and leave the stale one on disk.
